@page "/ui/share/node/{token}"
@model PetBox.Web.Pages.ShareNodeModel
@{
	ViewData["Title"] = (Model.Node?.Title ?? "Shared") + " — PetBox";
	ViewData["BodyClass"] = "min-h-full p-6";
	Layout = "_PublicLayout";
}
@* The public, anonymous face of ONE task node (spec `node-share`, work node-share-public-page).
   Reuses the two data-only partials the signed-in node page uses (_MdBody, _CommentThread) — they
   take a model and never touch User — so a shared node renders with the same markdown pipeline and
   the same thread shape as the private page, rather than a second renderer that would drift.

   THE CONFINEMENT (spec `node-share-confinement`) is in what is NOT passed down:

     * NodeRefs and MemoryRefs are left NULL. That is the whole leak defence and it is deliberate,
       not an omission: with a resolution map the renderer turns `[[slug]]` into a LINK to a node
       this reader cannot open AND spells the target's TITLE into the anchor text — publishing a
       private node's name to a stranger who was granted one node. With the map absent, the
       renderer leaves every mention literal (node-ref-autolink's own documented miss behaviour),
       so `[[slug]]` and memory keys stay plain text. IMarkdownRenderer itself is untouched — the
       page withholds the data rather than the renderer growing a "public" mode nobody could audit.

     * ShowAddForm: false. This is _CommentThread's existing "am I on the node's own authoring
       surface?" switch, and passing it false here is what suppresses BOTH the add/reply forms and
       the per-comment `share` button (see that partial's own note — a reader of a shared link must
       not be able to mint links of their own). NodeShareUiTests pins it.

     * ReadOnly: true, which is a SECOND and separate switch, added by this card. ShowAddForm alone
       was NOT enough and was believed to be: it gates the root add form and the share button, but
       every per-comment reply/edit/delete control rendered unconditionally — so the first anonymous
       render of this page served delete buttons, an antiforgery token, the node's internal NodeId in
       a hidden field, and every comment body a second time inside an editable textarea. The two
       flags stay separate because the board's LIST views pass ShowAddForm:false and must KEEP their
       inline edit/reply/delete; only this page is genuinely read-only.

     * NodeUrl: null (the default). The copy-a-permalink button builds an in-app URL that only a
       signed-in reader can open; the native `#comment-{id}` hash anchors still work here for free.

     * CommentRefs: NOT null, and that is the interesting one. `[[#comment]]` references
       (comment-slug-and-refs) point INSIDE this very page, so blanking the map would be the wrong
       answer — a reader of a full-thread share should be able to follow a body's reference to the
       segment printed below it. What is withheld instead is the map's CONTENT: ShareNodeModel
       builds it from `Thread`, the comments this page actually renders, so a reference to anything
       outside the grant resolves to nothing and stays plain text. scope=body publishes no comments
       and therefore an empty map; scope=comment publishes exactly one, so a reference to a
       NEIGHBOURING comment neither links into a UI this reader cannot open nor discloses that the
       neighbour exists. Same mechanism as the two maps above — withhold data, not behaviour.

   The cut fields (OriginSessionId, OriginSessions, DecisionPending, Observation, Relations,
   Ancestors) are absent because ShareNodeModel.PublicNode has no property for them at all — there
   is nothing here to forget to leave out.

   Comment AUTHORS render as they are. That is the owner's explicit decision (work card, point 5):
   an attributed remark is the thing being shared, and anonymising it would publish a quote nobody
   said. *@
@if (Model.Node is { } node)
{
	@* NO width container, on purpose (owner decision): the public face of a node stretches exactly
	   like the PRIVATE one, ProjectHome/TaskBoardNode.cshtml, which has no max-w wrapper either.
	   The public LOG share's `max-w-6xl` is a deliberately different story, not a precedent. *@
	@* No breadcrumb, no board link, no "open in PetBox" — every one of those is an invitation
	   into a UI this reader has no account for, and the first two would disclose the node's
	   neighbourhood on top of it. *@
	<h1 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-1" data-testid="share-node-title">@node.Title</h1>

	<div class="flex items-baseline gap-2 flex-wrap text-xs opacity-60 mb-4" data-testid="share-node-meta">
		<span class="font-mono" data-testid="share-node-key">@node.Key</span>
		<span class="badge badge-xs badge-ghost" data-testid="share-node-status">@node.Status</span>
		@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(node.Type))
		{
			<span class="badge badge-xs badge-ghost" data-testid="share-node-type">@node.Type</span>
		}
		@if (node.Priority != 0)
		{
			<span data-testid="share-node-priority">P@(node.Priority)</span>
		}
		@foreach (var tag in node.Tags)
		{
			<span class="badge badge-xs badge-ghost">@tag</span>
		}
		@if (node.Updated is { } updated)
		{
			<time class="local-time font-mono" datetime="@updated.ToString("o")" data-testid="share-node-updated">@updated.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm")</time>
		}
	</div>

	@* scope=comment shows the comment ALONE: no node body, and (see the page model) no
	   neighbouring comments either. The title above stays — a quote with no indication of what
	   it is attached to is worse than useless — but the body it was written under does not. *@
	@if (Model.ShowBody)
	{
		@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(node.Body))
		{
			<partial name="_MdBody" model="@(new PetBox.Web.Pages.Shared.MdBodyModel { Body = node.Body, TestId = "share-node-body", CommitUrlTemplate = Model.CommitUrlTemplate, CommentRefs = Model.CommentRefs })" />
		}
		else
		{
			<p class="text-base opacity-40 italic" data-testid="share-node-body-empty">(no body)</p>
		}

		@if (node.Commits.Count > 0)
		{
			<div class="mt-3 flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap text-xs" data-testid="share-node-commits">
				@foreach (var sha in node.Commits)
				{
					<span class="badge badge-xs badge-ghost font-mono">@sha</span>
				}
			</div>
		}
	}

	@* Rendered for `comment` and `full`, skipped entirely for `body` — a token that publishes
	   the body must not even show an empty "Comments" heading, which would tell the reader a
	   discussion exists (or does not) that the grant said nothing about. *@
	@if (Model.Scope != PetBox.Core.Models.NodeShareScopes.Body)
	{
		<partial name="_CommentThread" model="@(new PetBox.Web.Pages.Shared.CommentThreadModel(Model.Thread, node.NodeId, Model.CommitUrlTemplate, ShowAddForm: false, ReadOnly: true, CommentRefs: Model.CommentRefs))" />
	}
}
